<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>EC2 Provisioning with Terraform</h1>
  <p>Automated the deployment of an AWS EC2 instance using Terraform, demonstrating the full Infrastructure as Code workflow.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>Terraform</span><span>EC2</span><span>IaC</span><span>AWS</span><span>HCL</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/terraform.png" alt="Terraform EC2 Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates using <strong>Terraform</strong> to provision cloud infrastructure. A single <code>main.tf</code> configuration file defines and deploys an <strong>EC2 instance</strong> on AWS — fully automated and repeatable.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Terraform Workflow</h3>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">1</div><p><strong>terraform init</strong> — Downloads the AWS provider plugin.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">2</div><p><strong>terraform validate</strong> — Checks configuration syntax.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">3</div><p><strong>terraform plan</strong> — Preview resources to be created.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">4</div><p><strong>terraform apply</strong> — Creates the EC2 instance in AWS.</p></div>
      <div class="step-item"><div class="step-num">5</div><p><strong>terraform destroy</strong> — Tears down all provisioned resources.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Defined infrastructure using <strong>HCL (HashiCorp Configuration Language)</strong>.</li>
      <li>Compared <strong>IaC vs manual AWS Console</strong> provisioning.</li>
      <li>Understood <strong>Terraform state files</strong> for tracking deployed resources.</li>
      <li>Appreciated how IaC improves <strong>repeatability, speed, and team collaboration</strong>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Notes & Best Practices</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Use <strong>variables.tf</strong> — avoid hardcoding credentials or values.</li>
      <li>Store state remotely in <strong>S3 with DynamoDB locking</strong> for teams.</li>
      <li>Organize with <strong>modules</strong> for reusable infrastructure components.</li>
      <li>Never commit <strong>AWS access keys</strong> — use IAM roles or environment variables.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

